# useScaleImageOptions

Turns the `scaleImage` option of a background wrapper (`true`, `false` or a partial object) into explicit settings for each zoom input: pinching with two fingers and turning the mouse wheel. `CropperBackgroundWrapper` uses it to configure `TransformableImage`.

## Signature

```ts
function useScaleImageOptions(scaleImage: ScaleImageOptions | boolean): DefinedScaleImageOptions;

interface ScaleImageOptions {
	touch?: boolean;
	wheel?: boolean | { ratio?: number };
	adjustStencil?: boolean;
}

interface DefinedScaleImageOptions {
	touch: boolean;
	wheel: boolean | { ratio: number };
}
```

## Parameters

| Input                       | Result                                     |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| `true`                      | `{ touch: true, wheel: { ratio: 0.1 } }`   |
| `false` or undefined        | `{ touch: false, wheel: false }`           |
| `{ wheel: false }`          | `{ touch: true, wheel: false }`            |
| `{ wheel: true }`           | `{ touch: true, wheel: { ratio: 0.1 } }`   |
| `{ wheel: { ratio: 0.2 } }` | `{ touch: true, wheel: { ratio: 0.2 } }`   |
| `{ touch: false }`          | `{ touch: false, wheel: { ratio: 0.1 } }`  |

In an object, a missing key is enabled, and `wheel: true` gets the default `ratio` of `0.1`, the zoom step per wheel tick. `adjustStencil` is accepted by the type but dropped from the result. To control whether zooming resizes the stencil, use the cropper's `transformImage` setting instead.

## Return value

A new `DefinedScaleImageOptions` object. Pass `touch` to `TransformableImage`'s `touchScale` and `wheel` to its `wheelScale`.

## When to call it

Anywhere. It is a pure function with no effects. When its input is a prop, wrap the call in `$derived`:

```ts
let { scaleImage = true }: CropperBackgroundWrapperProps = $props();

const scaleOptions = $derived(useScaleImageOptions(scaleImage));
```

## Example

See the custom background wrapper on the [useMoveImageOptions](/docs/hooks/useMoveImageOptions#example) page, which uses all three option helpers.

From the user's side, the same values are what `backgroundWrapperProps` accepts:

```svelte
<Cropper {src} backgroundWrapperProps={{ scaleImage: { wheel: { ratio: 0.2 } } }} />
```

## Differences from React

React memoizes the result with `useMemo`. Here it is a plain function, so wrap it in `$derived` when the input can change.
